    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting explanations based on a student's level and pace. They can break down complex topics into simpler steps, provide instant feedback, and even simulate interactive problem-solving sessions. For someone like me with lower secondary education, this could be a game-changer, making math less intimidating and more accessible."
